      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town once housed one of the oldest mosques in the United States, built by Muslim homesteaders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ross%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After 1929, the mosque fell into disrepair and was dismantled before a local family rebuilt it in 2005.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ross%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Immigrants from Syria and Lebanon, arriving under the Homestead Act in the late 19th century, founded the mosque community that shaped Ross's early culture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ross%2C_North_Dakota",
